<title>NETHERLANDS: DUTCH PTT SEES NO TNT JOBS TRAUMA.</title>
<headline>DUTCH PTT SEES NO TNT JOBS TRAUMA.</headline>
<dateline>GRONINGEN, Netherlands 1997-03-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dutch post and telecoms group PTT Nederland NV (Dutch PTT) said on Tuesday major job cuts were unlikely as it restructured TNT the Australian transport company it recently acquired.</p>
<p>&quot;I don't see major problems in jobs (during the restructuring),&quot; said PTT Post head Ad Scheepbouwer following a results news conference.</p>
<p>He added that Dutch PTT was keen to integrate the logistics, domestic express, national express and international mail operations of TNT but would not be drawn on the fate of businesses which did not fit within Dutch PTT's scope.</p>
<p>&quot;Look at the TNT annual report and see which (business) is not within the boundaries,&quot; he said when pressed for details.</p>
<p>&quot;I'm looking at it...I have no wish to advertise those units not within our scope before we've told the employees,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam Newsroom +31 20 504 5000</p>
</text>
